---
layout: base.njk
title: PNW Insects
permalink: /index.html
description: "Photographs, descriptions, distribution maps, and identification tools for the insect fauna of British Columbia, Washington, Oregon, Idaho, and western Montana."
---
<section class="banner">
  <img class="banner-img" src="/images/banner-damselfly.jpg" alt="A blue-and-black damselfly resting on a bright green leaf">
  <div class="banner-scrim"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="banner-copy">
      <h1>PNW Insects</h1>
      <p>Photographs, descriptions, distribution maps, and identification tools for the region&rsquo;s insect fauna</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <span class="banner-credit">Photo: J. Williams</span>
</section>

<main class="wrap">
  <div class="columns">

    <section class="intro">
      <h2>Focus</h2>
      <p>
        Built on a foundation of collaboration among entomologists and institutions across the
        region, PNW Insects features comprehensive, information on select insect groups for
        British Columbia, Washington, Oregon, Idaho, and western Montana. We pair specimen
        photographs with detailed species accounts full of identification tips, distribution maps
        based on expert-reviewed records, and life history information. Our interactive
        identification tools and checklists make this site a powerful resource for anyone
        interested in the region&rsquo;s insects.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="resources">
      <h2 class="section-head">Resources</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">More resources join the list as they are completed.</p>

      <div class="cards">
        {% for resource in resources %}
        <a class="card" href="{{ resource.url }}">
          <div class="thumb">
            <img src="/images/{{ resource.image }}" alt="{{ resource.alt }}">
          </div>
          <div class="body">
            <h3>{{ resource.name }}</h3>
            <p class="count"><span class="badge">{{ resource.badge }}</span></p>
            <p>{{ resource.description }}</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</main>
